# Clean Architecture – Layered by Circles

## Project Structure Mapping

- **Domain Layer** (`Sonny.Application.Domain`) = Enterprise Business Rules (Inner Circle)
- **UseCases Layer** (`Sonny.Application.UseCases`) = Application Business Rules
- **Infrastructure Layer** (`Sonny.Application.Infrastructure`) = Interface Adapters (Framework Implementations)
- **Presentation Layer** (`Sonny.Application.Presentation`) = Interface Adapters (UI)
- **Application Layer** (`Sonny.Application`) = Entry Point / Host (Frameworks & Drivers)

## 1. Domain Layer (`Sonny.Application.Domain`)

**Includes:** Entities, Service Interfaces, Exceptions, Managers, SelectionFilters, Preprocessors

**⚠️ CRITICAL RESTRICTIONS:**
- ❌ **MUST NOT** use Revit API
- ❌ **MUST NOT** reference Revit packages
- ❌ **MUST NOT** know about ViewModels, UI, or frameworks
- ✅ **MUST** be completely framework-agnostic

## 2. UseCases Layer (`Sonny.Application.UseCases`)

**Includes:** Interactors, Interactor Interfaces, Application Services

**Rule:** Each feature requires an interactor

**⚠️ CRITICAL RESTRICTIONS:**
- ❌ **MUST NOT** use Revit API
- ❌ **MUST NOT** reference Revit packages
- ❌ **MUST NOT** depend on Infrastructure or Presentation layers
- ✅ **MUST** depend only on Domain layer

## 3. Infrastructure Layer (`Sonny.Application.Infrastructure`)

**Includes:** Domain interface implementations, Feature implementations, Revit services

**⚠️ RESTRICTIONS:**
- ✅ **CAN** use Revit API
- ✅ **CAN** reference Revit packages
- ✅ **CAN** reference Domain layer
- ❌ **MUST NOT** Presentation layers

## 4. Presentation Layer (`Sonny.Application.Presentation`)

**Includes:** ViewModels, Views, UI Services

**⚠️ RESTRICTIONS:**
- ✅ **CAN** reference UseCases and Domain layers
- ❌ **MUST NOT** reference Infrastructure layer directly
- ❌ **MUST NOT** use Revit API directly

## 5. Application Layer (`Sonny.Application`)

**Includes:** Commands, Host (DI setup), Ribbon, Modules

**⚠️ RESTRICTIONS:**
- ✅ **CAN** reference all layers
- ✅ **CAN** use Revit API (entry point)

## Dependency Rule

**Dependencies always point inward:**

```
Application → Infrastructure, Presentation, UseCases, Domain
Presentation → UseCases, Domain
Infrastructure → UseCases, Domain
UseCases → Domain
Domain → (nothing)
```

**Forbidden:**
- Domain → any other layer
- UseCases → Infrastructure, Presentation
- Presentation → Infrastructure

## CRITICAL: Revit API Restrictions

**⚠️ ABSOLUTE RULE - NEVER VIOLATE:**

- **Domain & UseCases Layers**
  - ❌ **MUST NOT** use Revit API
  - ❌ **MUST NOT** reference Revit packages
  - ✅ **MUST** use only Domain interfaces and entities

- **Infrastructure Layer**
  - ✅ **CAN** use Revit API
  - ✅ **CAN** use Library

**Why:** Domain and UseCases must be testable without Revit and framework-agnostic.

## Documentation Rules

- **Document interfaces only** - Interfaces require full XML documentation
- Classes/implementations don't need documentation unless complex logic
